{"segs": ["PA_ja_172:0.4"], "en": "2. The Daddara Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_172:1.1", "PA_ja_172:1.2"], "en": "“Who is it that makes the mountain Daddara resound with a great noise?”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_172:1.3"], "en": "The lions did not roar back at him, thinking,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_172:1.4"], "en": "\"Who indeed is this overlord of beasts?", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_172:2.1"], "en": "\"He is the lowest among the species of deer,\" [they said].", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_172:2.2"], "en": "\"The jackal is crying out, dear one;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_172:2.3", "PA_ja_172:2.4"], "en": "the lions, loathing his birth, wait in silence.\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
